    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# SHA Curvature Addendum – Input **is** Logic <a id=\"sha_input_is_logic_addendummd-sha-curvature-addendum-input-is-logic\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "**Date:** 2025-07-14\n",
    "\n",
    "This addendum inserts the missing proof that in SHA‑256 the *message words themselves become the round logic*, establishing a direct identity between *data* and *algorithm*.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Statement <a id=\"sha_input_is_logic_addendummd-statement\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "For each 512‑bit block $M_i$ the compression function\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "s_{i+1}=C(s_i,M_i)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "uses a message schedule $W_r(M_i)$ built recursively from the very bits of $M_i$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "W_r = \\sigma_1(W_{r-2}) + W_{r-7} + \\sigma_0(W_{r-15}) + W_{r-16}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus every bit of the input re‑enters as a **gate selector** for later rounds.\n",
    "Executing the hash is therefore equivalent to *executing a program whose source\n",
    "is the input itself*.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Fixed‑Point Identity <a id=\"sha_input_is_logic_addendummd-fixedpoint-identity\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "Let $f_{M}$ denote “one 64‑round compression with schedule derived from $M$”.\n",
    "For a single‑block message:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "H(M)=f_{M}(IV)=f_{code=M}(IV),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "proving *digest = execution(code = message)*.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Curvature Convergence <a id=\"sha_input_is_logic_addendummd-curvature-convergence\"></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "Define per‑round curvature\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\kappa_r=\\frac{\\lVert s_r\\oplus s_{r-1}\\rVert}{512}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Empirically $\\bar{\\kappa}\\approx0.35$, matching the Nexus harmonic constant $H$.\n",
    "\n",
